#. Tag: title
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the &PHP; Debugger"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With &quantaplus; version 3.3, the debugger handling was reimplemented. The "
"support for the now obsolete &PHP; (3) builtin debugger and was dropped, as "
"was the support for the dbg debugger. Instead, a general debug plugin system "
"was developed, to allow different plugin implementations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Currently only one plugin is available which adds support to use &gubed; "
"with &quantaplus;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To use a debugger for your project, open the project settings and chose a "
"suitable debugger plugin. To alter debugger specific settings, press the "
"'Options' button next to the debugger plugin drop down."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid "General usage"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:51
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once a project has a debugger activated, a few additional items will appear "
"in the &quantaplus; user interface:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid "Debugger menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A new menu will appear where you can reach most of the debugger "
"functionality."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "Debugger toolbar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid "A toolbar with access to the most common debugging commands."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "Variables toolview"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A toolview where the contents of watched variables is showed. Appears in the "
"left dock by default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid "Breakpoints toolview"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A toolview where all the breakpoints, line and conditional, are listed. "
"Appears in the bottom dock by default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "Debug Output toolview"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A toolview where the output (as in HTML) of the debugger is shown. Appears "
"in the bottom dock by default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on what the debugger plugin supports, all or a subset of the "
"following functionality will be available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Debug</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Session</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Start Session</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This action is used to connect to the debugger if that is required, or tell "
"the plugin to start listening for debug requests. This action is triggered "
"by default when a project using a debugger is opened, so usually you don't "
"need to care about it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Debug</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Session</guimenuitem> <guimenuitem>End "
"Session</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The opposite of <menuchoice> <guimenu>Debug</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Session</"
"guimenuitem> <guimenuitem>Start Session</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>. Closes "
"a connection to the debugger or stops listening for requests."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Debug</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Execution</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Send HTTP Request</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sends a HTTP request to the server to initiate a debug request. Using this "
"action is equivalent to using a browser to look at the current document. The "
"output of the request ends up in the Debug Output dock."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Debug</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Execution</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Pause</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid "Pauses a running script"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Debug</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Execution</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Run</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Tells the debugger to start executing the script and send information about "
"watched variables and current line of execution as it goes along. If this is "
"done while a script is paused, execution will proceed. If it's done before a "
"debug request is initiated, the script will start running as soon as the "
"request is initiated."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Debug</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Execution</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Leap</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Tells the debugger to start executing the script without sending information "
"about watched variables and current line of execution. If this is done while "
"a script is paused, execution will proceed. If it's done before a debug "
"request is initiated, the script will start leaping as soon as the request "
"is initiated."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Debug</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Execution</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Step</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Tells the debugger to execute the next instruction in the script, without "
"stepping into functions or inclusions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Debug</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Execution</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Step Into</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Tells the debugger to execute the next instruction in the script, stepping "
"into functions or inclusions if possible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Debug</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Execution</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Step Out</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tells the debugger to execute until it escapes the current function."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Debug</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Execution</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Skip</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:268
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Tells the debugger to skip the next instruction and proceed to the next one "
"as if the current one didn't exist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:276
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Debug</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Execution</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Kill</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tells the debugger to kill the currently running script."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Debug</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Breakpoints</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Break when...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid "Opens a dialog where you can specify conditional breakpoints."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Debug</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Breakpoints</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Toggle breakpoint</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid "Toggles a line breakpoint at the line of the cursor in the current line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Debug</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Breakpoints</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Clear breakpoints</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid "Clears all the breakpoints."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Debug</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Variables</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Watch variable</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:345
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Opens a dialog where you can enter a variable or expression you wish to "
"watch. The value of the watch will appear in the variables tool view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Debug</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Variables</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Set value of variable</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid "Opens a dialog where you can enter a variable and a new value for it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:377
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kxsl;, the &XSL; Debugger"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kxsl; is the creation of Keith Isdale, as is this section of the "
"documentation. &kxsl; is a &kde; front-end and a KPart to <command>xsldbg</"
"command>, which you can find at http://xsldbg.sf.net along with many other "
"works by Keith."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To start &kxsl;, select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Plugins</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>&kxsl;</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: debugging-quanta.docbook:395
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please refer to the &kxsl; documentation for further information regarding "
"its usage."
msgstr ""

